course: dictionary
lesson: 16
title: The many faces of about
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «About» is a small word with several jobs, and the words around it show which job it is doing. In «the hyacinth macaw is about a metre long», about means roughly: the bird is near one metre, not exactly one metre. Swap in «roughly» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In «Being open about money stops mix-ups in families», about means on the subject of money. Ask yourself: what is the topic? The answer is money, so about is linking the words to that topic.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in another word. If «roughly», «on the subject of» or «just going to» fits the sentence and still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: About can mean roughly or nearly, as in «about 36.5 to 37.5 degrees Celsius».
fact: About can mean on the subject of, as in «a book about dinosaurs» or «being open about money».
fact: «Be about to» means be just going to do something, as in «I was about to call you».
fact: About can mean here and there, as in children running about the yard.
fact: «Up and about» means out of bed and active again after being ill. In formal writing, «about» is often replaced by «concerning» or «regarding».
exercise: «The hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.» What does about mean here? | Exactly one metre | *Roughly, nearly one metre | Around and around | Far away from
exercise: «Being open about money stops mix-ups in families.» In this sentence, about means | *On the subject of | Just going to | Roughly | Running here and there
exercise: Which sentence uses about to mean just going to do something? | *I was about to call you. | The book is about dinosaurs. | Children were running about the yard. | Writing was invented about 5,200 years ago.
test: «Writing was invented separately in Mesopotamia about 5,200 years ago.» What does about mean here? | On the subject of | *Roughly, around | Exactly | Up and about
test: «Children were running about the yard.» What does about mean here? | Just going to start | *All around, here and there | On the subject of | Nearly finished
exam: Which formal word could replace about in «a story about a brave girl»? | up and about | be about to | *concerning | approximately 
